# The API image is built with `context: ../apps/api` (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml),
# and Docker reads .dockerignore from the CONTEXT root — not the repository root.
# The root .dockerignore therefore never applied to this build, which is how 565
# macOS AppleDouble files reached a production image.
#
# `._foo.py` sidecars are binary, they match *.py, and alembic's migration loader
# tries to parse every .py in versions/ — failing with "source code string cannot
# contain null bytes" and naming no file. Python's glob skips dot-files, so they
# are also invisible to the obvious "scan for null bytes" check.
._*
.DS_Store

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
